{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "18", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "12", "M": "13", "S": "50"}}, "news": [{"title": "Delhi: Seelampur, Sultanpuri and Lajpat Nagar JJ clusters set for redevelopment", "para": "The Delhi Urban Shelter Improvement Board is launching a redevelopment project for jhuggi-jhopri clusters via public-private collaborations. This entails hiring a transaction adviser for feasibility assessments and choosing a private developer to spearhead the project. The goal is to elevate living standards for slum inhabitants while optimizing land use.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/delhi-seelampur-sultanpuri-and-lajpat-nagar-jj-clusters-set-for-redevelopment/135028614?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-292826/135028614.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Delhi civic body's survey identifies over 21,000 properties operating commercially in residential zones", "para": "The Municipal Corporation of Delhi has identified over 21,000 properties engaged in commercial activities within residential areas. Actions against violations of land-use norms have been initiated following a Supreme Court order. Approximately 12,000 properties have paid conversion charges, while 9,000 remain non-compliant. Sealing actions have begun in specific zones, including Central and Rohini. The survey will continue in unauthorized colonies and areas benefiting from the PM-UDAY scheme.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/delhi-civic-bodys-survey-identifies-over-21000-properties-operating-commercially-in-residential-zones/135028590?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-334916/135028590.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "commercial"}, {"title": "India Cements' profit multifold to \u20b938.82 crore in Q2 FY27", "para": "India Cements Ltd, part of the UltraTech Cement group, has reported a remarkable surge in its net profit for the September quarter, soaring to Rs 38.82 crore from Rs 8.81 crore the previous year. Revenue from operations increased to Rs 1,142.03 crore, while domestic sales volume grew by 16.2 percent, reaching 2.83 million tonnes. Furthermore, the board has greenlit the relocation of the registered office from Tamil Nadu to Maharashtra.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/cement/india-cements-profit-multifold-to-38-82-crore-in-q2-fy27/135028352?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-727226/135028352.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "cement"}]}